window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>“Narrator Priestley excels at voicing Carton's interiority.” <i>— AudioFile </i></b><br><b><i><br>Jonathan Strange &amp; Mr Norrell </i>meets <i>A Tale of Two Cities</i> in H. G. Parry’s <i>A Far Better Thing</i>, a heart-rending fantasy of faery revenge set during the French Revolution.<br></b><b><br>Most Anticipated SSF Books 2025—<i>The Nerd Daily</i>, <i>BookPage</i><br></b><br><i>I feared this was the best of times; I hoped it could not get any worse.</i><br><br>The faeries stole Sydney Carton as a child, and made him a mortal servant of the Faery Realm. Now, he has a rare opportunity for revenge against the fae and Charles Darnay, the changeling left in his stead.<br><br>It will take magic and cunning—cold iron and Realm silver—to hide his intentions from humans and fae and bring his plans to fruition.<br><br>Shuttling between London and Paris during the Reign of Terror, generations of violence-begetting-violence lead him to a heartbreaking choice in the shadow of the guillotine.<br><br><b>A Macmillan Audio production from Tor Books.</b></p>"; 
